Validated — schema-legal, one update, nothing written.

## The answer: keep both slots, add one key

```json5
{
  plugins: {
    slots: {
      memory:        "memory-lancedb-pro",  // unchanged
      contextEngine: "lossless-claw"        // unchanged
    },
    entries: {
      "lossless-claw": {
        config: { hostFallbackMode: "capture-only" }   // ← the only change
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**Why this is the answer and not a compromise:** `capture-only` declares exactly `[bootstrap, after-turn, maintain]` — the intersection. Embedded (6 caps) and codex (7) are proper supersets, so all three pass. And the requirement value *only* controls whether the assert throws; it never controls whether `assemble()` runs. So codex and embedded keep the **full** lossless lifecycle unchanged — the degradation is per-host, applying only to CLI runs, which never had assembly available anyway.

**First, a correction.** I told you subagents spawned from a claude-cli turn would still fail on `thread-bootstrap-projection`. That was wrong. I checked every call site: all four pass `operation: "agent-run"`, and `subagent-spawn` and `manual-compact` have **zero** call sites — declared but never enforced. Subagents are fine.

| | embedded | codex | **claude-cli** |
|---|---|---|---|
| Memory recall | Full | Full | **Full** — same ungated hook |
| Memory capture | Full | Full | **Full** |
| Context assembly | Full LCM | Full LCM | **Degraded** — `assemble()` never runs; recall via `lcm_grep`/`lcm_expand` tools |
| Transcript capture | Full | Full | **Works** — `lcm.db` keeps growing |
| Compaction | lossless | lossless | Claude Code's own (backend declares `ownsNativeCompaction`) |
| Subagent spawn | Works | Works | **Works** |

**You lose nothing that currently works.** `assemble()` has never run on the CLI path — `cli-runner.ts` doesn't import it. The strict requirement wasn't protecting a working feature; it was converting an unavoidable degradation into a hard crash.

**Why not `legacy`** (the seemingly safer option): lossless stops being the *selected* engine, so `ingest`/`afterTurn` stop being driven and **`lcm.db` freezes** — your DAG stops growing everywhere, including on codex. Strictly worse.

**Keep `memory-lancedb-pro`.** The memory slot has no capability gate at all — `hostRequirements` exists only on `ContextEngineInfo`. Memory was never part of this problem, and it's verified working on all three paths. No reason to touch 713 entries.

**Separate follow-up worth knowing:** your lossless config pins `summaryModel: openai/gpt-5.6-luna` and `expansionModel: openai/gpt-5.6-terra` with no fallbacks — so lossless's own summarization still dies during a codex outage. This fix doesn't address that. I haven't verified whether its `fallbackProviders` accepts a claude-cli-backed model, so I'm not prescribing a value yet.

**Honestly unproven:** nobody has executed `capture-only` end-to-end — it's verified by construction (constants, gate logic, schema validation), not by a live turn. And plugin config is parsed at plugin init, so this likely needs a gateway restart to take effect.

Rollback is `/data/.openclaw/openclaw.json.bak` (three backups present). Want me to apply it? Your cron is still failing hourly, and this would restore autonomous runs without waiting for the Codex reset.
